/P 120 0 R
/E (Phishing is a type of cyber attack where criminals impersonate trusted entities through deceptive emails, messages, or websites to steal sensitive information. These attacks often create urgency, using tactics like fake account warnings, payment requests, or credential verification demands. Phishing remains one of the most common and effective attack vectors, responsible for over 90% of data breaches. Understanding how to identify these threats is critical for protecting organizational security and personal data.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [12]
>>
